# CODEOWNERS
#
# High-risk paths below require review from a qualified code owner before a
# PR can merge into main. These are enforced via the repository's branch
# protection rule "Require review from Code Owners" (see SECURITY.md for the
# rationale and prior-issue history).

/src/soroban/                        @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers
/src/common/stellar-signature.ts     @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers
/prisma/schema.prisma                @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers
/src/soroban/signer.service.ts       @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers

# Supply chain (issue #467). A workflow change is a change to what runs with
# this repository's credentials and OIDC identity: the signing identity in
# .github/workflows/cd.yml is the *only* thing standing between a maintainer
# account compromise and an attacker-signed production image. CODEOWNERS is
# what makes a swapped action SHA, a widened `permissions:` block or a new
# `id-token: write` a review question rather than a diff line.
#
# NOTE: all workflows, and dependabot, were removed in the CI cleanup, so these
# two patterns currently match nothing. They are kept deliberately as a
# tripwire rather than deleted: the day anyone re-adds a workflow or an
# automated dependency updater — reintroducing cd.yml and image signing being
# the case that matters — it lands in security review automatically. Deleting
# them would quietly remove that.
.github/workflows/                  @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers
/.github/dependabot.yml              @vortex-protocol/security-reviewers
